quran[5]{c,v,t}:
  66,8,"O believers! Turn to Allah in sincere repentance. Perhaps your Lord shall absolve you of your misdeeds and admit you into the Gardens with rivers flowing beneath them. That Day, Allah will not disgrace the Prophet (blessings and peace be upon him) and the believers with him. Their light will shine, spreading before them and on their right. They will say: ‘Our Lord, complete our light for us and forgive us! Surely, You are All-Capable of everything.’"
  66,9,"O Prophet! Struggle against the disbelievers and the hypocrites and be firm with them. Their refuge is Hell, and it is an evil destination."
  66,10,"Allah has given an example for the disbelievers: The wife of Nuh (Noah) and the wife of Lut (Lot). They both were under two of Our righteous servants, but they betrayed them. So, they did not benefit them against Allah in any way. It was said (to them): ‘Enter the Fire (the both of you) along with (other) incomers.’*"
  66,11,"Allah has given an example for the believers: The wife of Pharaoh, when she said: ‘My Lord! Build for me a house in Paradise near Your presence and deliver me from Pharaoh and his (evil) conduct. Save me from the wrongdoing people.’*"
  66,12,"And (there is also the example of) Maryam (Mary), the daughter of ‘Imran, who guarded her chastity well. So We breathed in her (womb) through Our Spirit (Gabriel). She confirmed the Words of her Lord and His (revealed) Scriptures, and she was one of the devoutly obedient."
